  "_comment": [
    "Work queue for scripts/parity_model_sweep.py — the resumable CPU<->Vulkan parity sweep.",
    "",
    "This file is DATA. Add a model by appending an object to `models`; never edit the harness.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  id           (required) stable slug — the key used in the state file. Never rename.",
    "  repo         (required) Hugging Face repo id. Downloaded into the HF hub cache.",
    "  file         (required) file name inside that repo (the GGUF).",
    "  filter       (required) narrow `dotnet test --filter` expression. MUST be narrow:",
    "               the full unit suite takes ~57 min and hangs, and any filter containing",
    "               the substring 'Quant' drags in the whole Vulkan GPU suite (46+ min).",
    "  env          (optional) DOTLLM_* env var the test reads; set to the fetched path.",
    "  stage_path   (optional) conventional path the test falls back to when `env` is unset.",
    "               The harness HARDLINKS the hub-cache blob here (never copies) and removes",
    "               the hardlink during cleanup.",
    "  size_bytes   (optional) fallback size used for smallest-first ordering when the HF API",
    "               is unreachable. The harness prefers the live API size.",
    "  timeout_sec  (optional) per-model test timeout, default 1800.",
    "  available    (optional, default true) set false for a model that cannot be fetched;",
    "               the harness records it as `skipped` without touching the network.",
    "  skip_reason  (optional) why `available` is false.",
    "  notes        (optional) free text, echoed into the log.",
    "",
    "Derived from the actual fixture resolution in tests/DotLLM.Tests.Integration/ —",
    "grep for `envVar:` / `conventional:` there if a test's fixture contract changes."
  ],

